    Redesign as a wide dashboard; add meal-planning and workout-program boards
    
    Dashboard redesign:
    - New responsive shell: fixed sidebar + wide multi-column content on
      desktop/tablet, original bottom-nav single-column layout preserved on
      mobile (same routes and pages, different layout past the md breakpoint)
    - Dashboard reworked from one long vertical stack into a grid of panels
      (main column + a Coach/Priorities right rail on wide screens)
    
    Meal planning board:
    - Weekly calendar grid (day columns x meal-type rows) replacing the old
      flat list view — drag cards between cells (desktop) or tap "+" to
      search and add (works everywhere, including touch)
    - New backend endpoints: add/move/remove a single meal-plan item, and
      add directly from a Food with macros auto-scaled by quantity
    
    Workout programs:
    - New schema: WorkoutProgram / WorkoutProgramDay / WorkoutProgramExercise
      / ProgramEnrollment, plus muscleGroup/description on Exercise and a
      program-day link on WorkoutSession for adherence tracking
    - Exercise library seed: 65 exercises (bodyweight-heavy, plus strength,
      resistance bands, kettlebells, mobility) with muscle group + form notes
    - 3 starter programs built from that library: 4-Week Bodyweight
      Foundations, 3-Week Kettlebell Conditioning, 2-Week Resistance Band
      Starter — enroll, see today's workout, mark complete to auto-advance
      through the program
    - New Programs page: today's workout, browse/enroll, full week x day
      program board, and a searchable/filterable exercise library browser
    
    All of it validated against a real local Postgres (not just typecheck):
    migrations applied cleanly, every new endpoint smoke-tested end to end,
    and every page + the new drag/drop and modals verified in an actual
    browser with zero console errors.

