    Add self-hosted personal wellness dashboard app
    
    Full-stack weight-loss and wellness platform under wellness-app/, built
    for a home-server deployment behind Nginx with HTTPS:
    
    - Backend: Express + TypeScript + PostgreSQL (Prisma), JWT auth with
      httpOnly refresh cookies, rate limiting, audit logging. Domain services
      and REST routes for weight/body measurements, blood pressure & vitals
      (with user-defined target ranges, never diagnostic), nutrition/foods/
      recipes/meals, meal planning, grocery lists, pantry, exercise, habits,
      water/sleep/steps, goals, progress charts, and CSV/JSON/PDF export.
    - AI Coach: provider-agnostic abstraction (OpenAI, Ollama, or disabled)
      behind a single AIService, with a safety layer that forbids diagnosis
      or medication guidance, trend-based context building (not single-point
      reactions), conversational chat, daily/weekly/monthly insights, AI meal
      planning and substitutions, and a pantry "what can I make tonight"
      assistant. The app runs fully with AI disabled.
    - Frontend: React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind, mobile-first with a
      bottom nav (Home/Log/Meals/Coach/Progress), quick-action logging
      sheets, progress rings, trend charts (Recharts), and dark/light mode.
    - Infra: Docker Compose (frontend, backend, postgres, nginx, optional
      Ollama profile), production Nginx config (HTTPS, HSTS/CSP headers,
      rate limiting, WebSocket support, Postgres never exposed), backup/
      restore/self-signed-cert scripts, and a full installation README.
    
    Backend and frontend both typecheck and build cleanly; docker-compose
    config validated. Live container pulls from Docker Hub could not be
    tested in this sandbox (egress policy blocks the registry CDN host).
